1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,000
In the 2024.2 version, Cloud's component simulation has been improved, and the component will be affected by gravity and the interaction force of the panels.

2
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:20,000
These improvements also make the display effect of the component more realistic. At the same time, the stability of the component simulation has also been greatly improved.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,000
We will show the functions after the improvement through the component on this suit.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:40,000
First, we insert a component into the object window and attach it to the panel with a glue stick, then adjust its position.

5
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:51,000
When you use the right-click unit component, you can see that the simulation option has been increased in the right-click menu, and the state of the component simulation is also divided into freeze, activate, and counter-activate.

6
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Since the glue tool is used at this time, you can see that the component simulation has been improved.

7
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
The left-click unit component is unable to switch to freeze or activate.

8
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:04,000
When you use the right-click unit component to remove the glue, the three simulation states can be switched at this time.

9
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Select the activation option and start simulation.

10
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:15,000
After running the simulation, use the grab to drag the component, you can see that it is presented under the state of gravity and the interaction force of the panel.

11
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:22,000
The component will fall down a little due to gravity, and the interaction force between the panel and the panel will be hung by the panel.

12
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,000
The effect of the real component and the panel are the same.

13
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,000
The effect of the real component and the panel are the same.

14
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:31,000
And the right-click component editor has also been added to the simulation of the conflict thickness and rigidity.

15
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:37,000
You can adjust the conflict thickness between the component and the panel by entering the value.

16
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:44,000
In the previous version, the component that did not use the glue tool glue after running the simulation will not be affected by gravity.

17
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Therefore, it will remain in the original position and will not fall down in the direction of gravity.

18
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:54,000
In the component simulation, the connection is frozen, and it can be fixed to the component as in the previous version.

19
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Let's switch to the other component.

20
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Right-click the component, choose to freeze, and start simulation.

21
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,000
The component will not fall down under gravity.

22
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Using the grab to move the component, you can see that the interaction force between the component and the panel also exists.

23
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Unlike the activation, after the component is frozen, you can see that the rigidity in the right attribute editor window is gray.

24
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:21,000
This is because after the component is frozen, there will be no deformation.

25
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Therefore, the rigidity of the component cannot be changed.

26
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:31,000
According to the difference in the component type, in the 2024.2 version, the component will be transformed by the interaction force between the component and the panel.

27
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:35,000
First, the component must also be in the state of activation.

28
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Activate the component, check whether the rigidity simulated in the right attribute editor is used.

29
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Rigidity refers to the degree of rigidity of the component.

30
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,000
The default rigidity of the component is 50,000.

31
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,000
The minimum value is 5000.

32
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,000
The maximum value can be entered to 100,000.

33
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,000
Then, when we reduce the rigidity of the component to 50,000.

34
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Then, when we reduce the rigidity of the component to 50,000.

35
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,000
Turn on simulation.

36
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:58,000
You can see that the component is more likely to be pulled by the power of the panel, transform.

37
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:05,000
On the other hand, if you want to set it as a solid component that is not easy to transform, you can increase its rigidity.

38
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:09,000
You can adjust its rigidity according to the real effect of the component.

39
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:13,000
Finally, right-click the component, select the reverse activation simulation.

40
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Turn on simulation.

41
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,000
The component is kept in its original position.

42
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,000
Use your hand to grab the component.

43
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,000
You can see the interaction between the component and the panel.

44
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,000
and the interaction effect of the 3D window has also disappeared.

45
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,000
From this version,

46
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:28,000
the add-on in the 3D window that does not use the glue stick attached to the board

47
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:32,000
can also show the effect of the add-on in the gravity function.

48
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:36,000
We first right-click the add-on and select Activate.

49
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:39,000
Then select the add-on in the object window.

50
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Find the option of Weight at the bottom of the attribute editor.

51
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:46,000
At this time, the weight of the add-on is 7.6 grams.

52
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Simulate to check the effect of the add-on under the current weight.

53
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:54,000
Then change the weight of the add-on to 50 grams,

54
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:55,000
and then simulate.

55
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:59,000
You can find that the add-on is more in the gravity function.

56
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,000
The above is the new function of our add-on simulation.

57
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:07,000
It should be noted that the current add-on simulation is only suitable for CPU simulation.

58
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Based on this,

59
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:13,000
you can set the hardness or weight of the add-on according to the type of add-on you want,

60
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:18,000
and adjust it to make the display effect of the add-on simulation more realistic.

